{
  "case_id": "2020-19-5807",
  "document_hash": "aa2a60ff15d80f6fe8e5706e9f0dc75121eb9e981c7c0b63b21fe3c301151192",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-5807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa2a60ff15d80f6fe8e5706e9f0dc75121eb9e981c7c0b63b21fe3c301151192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa2a60ff15d8-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "At the time, Louisiana law permitted non-unanimous jury verdicts if at least 10 of the 12 jurors found the defendant guilty."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-5807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa2a60ff15d80f6fe8e5706e9f0dc75121eb9e981c7c0b63b21fe3c301151192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa2a60ff15d8-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Edwards fled a federal habeas corpus petition, arguing that the non-unanimous jury verdict violated his constitutional right to a unanimous jury."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Edwards",
      "case_id": "2020-19-5807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa2a60ff15d80f6fe8e5706e9f0dc75121eb9e981c7c0b63b21fe3c301151192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa2a60ff15d8-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Edwards now argues that the Ramos jury-unanimity rule applies retroactively on federal collateral review."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2020-19-5807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa2a60ff15d80f6fe8e5706e9f0dc75121eb9e981c7c0b63b21fe3c301151192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa2a60ff15d8-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Christopher G. Michel argued the cause for the United States as amicus curiae urging affrmance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2020-19-5807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa2a60ff15d80f6fe8e5706e9f0dc75121eb9e981c7c0b63b21fe3c301151192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa2a60ff15d8-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ramos held that a state jury must be unanimous to convict a defendant of a serious offense. In so holding, Ramos announced a new rule."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2020-19-5807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa2a60ff15d80f6fe8e5706e9f0dc75121eb9e981c7c0b63b21fe3c301151192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa2a60ff15d8-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Having determined that Ramos announced a new rule requiring jury unanimity, we must consider whether that new rule falls within an exception for watershed rules of criminal procedure that apply retroactively on federal collateral review."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2020-19-5807",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "aa2a60ff15d80f6fe8e5706e9f0dc75121eb9e981c7c0b63b21fe3c301151192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa2a60ff15d8-0002-0000",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And criminal defend- ants as a group are better off under Ramos and today's deci- sion, taken together, than they would have been if Justice Kagan's dissenting view had prevailed in Ramos."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-5807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa2a60ff15d80f6fe8e5706e9f0dc75121eb9e981c7c0b63b21fe3c301151192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa2a60ff15d8-0003-0000",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the answer was nearly always yes, one important exception existed both here and in England. A habeas court could grant relief if the court of conviction lacked jurisdiction over the defendant or his offense."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-5807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa2a60ff15d80f6fe8e5706e9f0dc75121eb9e981c7c0b63b21fe3c301151192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa2a60ff15d8-0003-0001",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "a federal court was powerless to revisit those proceedings unless the state court had acted without jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-5807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa2a60ff15d80f6fe8e5706e9f0dc75121eb9e981c7c0b63b21fe3c301151192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa2a60ff15d8-0003-0002",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "that: The writ of habeas corpus does not authorize federal courts to reopen a judgment issued by a court of competent jurisdiction once it has become fnal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-5807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa2a60ff15d80f6fe8e5706e9f0dc75121eb9e981c7c0b63b21fe3c301151192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa2a60ff15d8-0004-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A verdict, taken from eleven, [i]s no verdict at all,\u201d this Court proclaimed just last Term. Ramos v. Louisiana, 590 U. S. \u2013\u2013\u2013, \u2013\u2013\u2013 \u2013 \u2013\u2013\u2013 (2020) (internal quotation marks omitted)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-5807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa2a60ff15d80f6fe8e5706e9f0dc75121eb9e981c7c0b63b21fe3c301151192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa2a60ff15d8-0004-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A watershed rule, we held, is \u201cimplicit in the concept of ordered liberty.\u201d Teague, 489 U. S., at 311 (plurality opinion) (internal quotation marks omitted)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-5807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa2a60ff15d80f6fe8e5706e9f0dc75121eb9e981c7c0b63b21fe3c301151192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa2a60ff15d8-0004-0004",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Jury unanimity, the Court pronounced, is an \u201cessential element[ ]\u201d of the jury trial right, and thus is \u201cfundamental to the American scheme of justice.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-5807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa2a60ff15d80f6fe8e5706e9f0dc75121eb9e981c7c0b63b21fe3c301151192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa2a60ff15d8-0004-0005",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When can the State punish a defendant for committing a crime? Return again to Ramos, this time going back to Blackstone: Only when \u201cthe truth of [an] accusation\u201d is \u201cconfrmed by the unanimous suffrage\u201d of a jury \u201cof his equals and neighbours.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-5807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa2a60ff15d80f6fe8e5706e9f0dc75121eb9e981c7c0b63b21fe3c301151192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa2a60ff15d8-0004-0007",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Two concurring opinions linked that history to current practice. \u201cIn light of the[ir] racist origins,\u201d Justice Kavanaugh stated, \u201cit is no surprise that non-unanimous juries can make a difference\u201d\u2014that \u201c[t]hen and now\u201d they can \u201cnegate the votes of black jurors, especially in cases with black defendants.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-5807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa2a60ff15d80f6fe8e5706e9f0dc75121eb9e981c7c0b63b21fe3c301151192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa2a60ff15d8-0004-0009",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A watershed rule, the Court said there, must go to the jury's \u201cdetermination of innocence or guilt.\u201d 489 U. S., at 313 (plurality opinion); see Beard, 542 U. S., at 417."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-5807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa2a60ff15d80f6fe8e5706e9f0dc75121eb9e981c7c0b63b21fe3c301151192",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa2a60ff15d8-0005-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "fundamental\u2014if a verdict rendered by a divided jury is \u201cno verdict at all\u201d\u2014then Thedrick Edwards should not spend his life behind bars over two jurors' opposition. I respectfully dissent."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
